{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":262822,"duration_api_ms":262783,"num_turns":1,"result":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity with GNU reference binaries through differential testing.\n\n**Architecture:** Four stages (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/<utility>/` (implementations), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (shared formatting), `pkg/testutils/` (differential test harness), `magefiles/` (build targets, code generation boundary). Human operator owns specs; orchestrator owns synthesis.\n\n**Current state:** Working branch is spec-only. Generated code (4,586 LOC across 22 files including pkg/testutils, pkg/sys, pkg/format, cmd/ts, cmd/cat, cmd/wc, cmd/sponge) lives at `generation-merged` tags only. All `code_status` entries show `not started` on the working branch.\n\n**Release scope:** rel00.0 (Batch 0 — foundational infrastructure). Four use cases, all `spec_complete, not started`:\n- `rel00.0-uc001-magefiles` — magefiles/ is excluded from generation per DD7; only `cmd/version` is generated\n- `rel00.0-uc002-format` — pkg/format/\n- `rel00.0-uc003-sys` — pkg/sys/\n- `rel00.0-uc004-testutils` — pkg/testutils/\n\n**Priority reasoning:** Among the three generatable library packages (format, sys, testutils), canonical ordering is alphabetical for equal-priority libraries: `pkg/format` < `pkg/sys` < `pkg/testutils`. pkg/format has no intra-project dependencies, making it the correct first task.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement pkg/format shared formatting library [rel00.0-uc002-format]\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/format component description, technology_choices, design_decisions DD3 and DD7)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc002-format.yaml (use case; follow the PRD reference inside to locate and read the format PRD before writing any code)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/format/columns.go\n        action: create\n        note: Column alignment functions for tabular output (ls -l style)\n      - path: pkg/format/color.go\n        action: create\n        note: ANSI escape code constants and file-type color lookup\n      - path: pkg/format/size.go\n        action: create\n        note: Human-readable byte-count formatting with K/M/G suffixes\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement column alignment that computes per-column widths from a 2D string slice and pads each cell to produce uniform column widths across all rows, matching ls -l tabular style per the format PRD\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement ANSI terminal color constants and a file-type color lookup function covering regular files, directories, symlinks, executables, sockets, named pipes, block devices, and character devices per the format PRD\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement human-readable size formatting that converts a uint64 byte count to a string with K, M, or G suffix using powers of 1024, matching GNU coreutils output format per the format PRD\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: pkg/format is a shared library imported by cmd/ packages -- no cmd/ package may duplicate formatting logic that belongs in pkg/format (ARCHITECTURE.yaml DD3)\n      - id: D2\n        text: Use only the Go standard library; golang.org/x/sys is the only external dependency permitted project-wide and pkg/format does not require it (ARCHITECTURE.yaml technology_choices)\n      - id: D3\n        text: All source files reside in package format with no sub-packages; file names must derive from the primary exported type or function group as specified in the format PRD (planning constitution P7)\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: go build ./pkg/format/... completes with no errors\n      - id: AC2\n        text: Column alignment function produces uniform per-column widths across all rows given a 2D string input where cells in the same column have varying lengths\n      - id: AC3\n        text: File-type color lookup returns a non-empty ANSI escape sequence for each of the eight file types listed in R2 and returns an empty string or reset sequence for unknown types\n      - id: AC4\n        text: Size formatting converts 1024 to a K-suffixed string, 1048576 to an M-suffixed string, and 1073741824 to a G-suffixed string per the format PRD specification\n      - id: AC5\n        text: golangci-lint passes on all pkg/format/ files with no warnings\n```","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"41869b0e-5172-4626-bb13-a1d0ee93eec5","total_cost_usd":0.5134434999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19072,"cache_read_input_tokens":15967,"output_tokens":15450,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19072,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":15450,"cacheReadInputTokens":15967,"cacheCreationInputTokens":19072,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.5134434999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"uuid":"7f3f6f9d-50b9-43aa-84c8-69328a7681a9"}
